# Backwards compatibility — only explicitly

The project is pre-release: there are no published versions and no external
clients. Breaking changes are made cleanly — without shims and fallbacks.

## Rules

- **Don't invent compat.** Version branches in parsers, env aliases,
  dual-format accept, "the old path just in case" — introduce only on the
  user's explicit request.
- **Break cleanly.** If a format / API / env changes — the old one is removed
  in the same task, not kept alive in parallel "for compatibility".
- **If compat seems needed** (rolling update, an external client, data in
  prod) — ask explicitly first, don't build it in silently.

## Precedent

Ticket v2/v3 + `ENET_LISTEN_PORT` alias + migration notes accumulated
silently and were cleaned up in `docs/plans/P28-drop-prerelease-compat.md`;
the policy is recorded in `docs/adr/0010-drop-prerelease-compat.md`.
